{"id":"chatcmpl-88aa4a3ab21783ef","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to list the three most serious problems from the codebase. Let me analyze the code carefully for correctness bugs, prioritizing by severity.\n\nLet me go through the code:\n\n1. **`cli.ts` - `main()` function: `loadRunnerConfig` and `loadDotEnvDefaults` ordering vs `applyRoleProfile`**\n\nIn `cli.ts`, the entry point does:\n```ts\nconst config = loadRunnerConfig();\nloadDotEnvDefaults();\nlet settled = false;\nconst argv = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst outPath = readFlag(argv, FLAG_OUT);\nconst agentType = resolveAgentType(argv);\napplyRoleProfile(config, agentType);\nconst tracing = initTracing();\n```\n\nBut `loadDotEnvDefaults()` is called AFTER `loadRunnerConfig()`. The README says:\n> `loadRunnerConfig()` seeds the `RUNNER_*` env vars listed below on startup,","signature":"4b75c6bacce443b9b486b0a49c889b24"}],"model":"qwen38-27b-mxfp4-dflash","stop_reason":"max_tokens","usage":{"input_tokens":1183,"output_tokens":200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5280,"cache_read_input_tokens":32560}}